    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"Grit Goblin\" is actually a really interesting phrase. it's definitely got that specific vibe i'm looking for. \n\ncan you lean into that a bit more? like, if we were to use that kind of imagery to describe the team's \"nature\"—not in a literal way, obviously, but as a way to talk about how we operate underneath the surface—how would you expand on it? if our team is a \"grit goblin\" type of group, what does that actually say about our work ethic, how we deal with problems, or how we interact with the bigger, more \"polished\" companies in our space?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
